!Series_summary	"We used RNA-seq to evaluate the transcriptomic changes induced in HN-SCC-151 cells treated with DMSO or the SUV420H1 inhibitor A-196/siNC (control) or siSUV420H1 siRNAs."
!Series_overall_design	"Bulk RNA-seq was performed to characterize transcriptional changes associated with SUV420H1 perturbation in HPV-negative HNSCC models. Human HPV-negative HN-SCC-151 cells were cultured in-vitro in three separate 10cm dishes per condition and were treated with SUV420H1-targeting siRNA or the SUV420H1 enzymatic inhibitor A-196 (2.5uM) for 6 days, and compared with matched non-targeting siRNA or DMSO-treated controls. In vivo, MOC1 control tumors (n=4) and Suv420h1 knockout MOC1 tumors (n=4) grown in C57BL/6 mice were analyzed by bulk RNA-seq."
